From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:02:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: open the PCI sysfs config file with PID 1's root

Since kernel 7.3 the true VFS root is an empty nullfs and kernel threads
resolve paths against it, so filp_open("/sys/...") from a kthread fails.
nv_pci_probe() runs asynchronously in a kthread, so nv_get_pci_sysfs_config()
never got the config file, nv_dynamic_power_available() returned false and
runtime D3 was reported "Not supported" even with NVreg_DynamicPowerManagement=2
and a working _PR3.

Borrow PID 1's fs root with scoped_with_init_fs() for the open when the
kernel provides it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
index 5c48eb82..96b02f6b 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 #include "nv-vgpu-vfio-interface.h"
 #endif
 #include <linux/completion.h>
+#include <linux/fs_struct.h>
 #include <linux/iommu.h>
 #include <linux/kthread.h>
 
@@ -439,7 +440,20 @@ static void nv_get_pci_sysfs_config
                    NV_PCI_SLOT_NUMBER(pci_dev));
     if (ret > 0 && ret < sizeof(filename))
     {
-        struct file *file = filp_open(filename, O_RDONLY, 0);
+        struct file *file;
+
+        /*
+         * Probe can run in a kthread. Since the kernel moved kthreads onto
+         * an empty nullfs root, path lookups from them fail unless they
+         * borrow PID 1's root, so do that when the kernel provides the
+         * helper.
+         */
+#if defined(scoped_with_init_fs)
+        scoped_with_init_fs()
+            file = filp_open(filename, O_RDONLY, 0);
+#else
+        file = filp_open(filename, O_RDONLY, 0);
+#endif
         if (!IS_ERR(file))
         {
 #if defined(NV_SEQ_READ_ITER_PRESENT)
